Version: 0.7
Description:
  The Seed Database section: generate a set of data.

  The rows it writes are ordinary rows. There is no separate universe, no provenance column and no
  per-set cleanup, because there is nothing to tell apart - during development the whole database is
  disposable and is reset wholesale when it needs to be.

  What this screen is for is the opposite problem: an empty installation cannot be judged. A
  catalogue with no courses, a dashboard with no figures and a table with no rows all look the same
  whether they work or not.

  Comments here are plain prose only: no angle brackets, no comment delimiters, no template tokens
  and no code.
Changelog:
  2026/09/09 23:35 SAST
  - Rebuilt without sets, tokens or cleanup; generation is what remains and what it was always for.
